<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Area of a plot from a map grid</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>On a map of scale \(1 : {@Sd@}\), the outline of [[if test="is(pl=0)"]]the compound of a school in Machakos[[elif test="is(pl=1)"]]a shamba near Nyeri[[elif test="is(pl=2)"]]a tea farm near Kericho[[elif test="is(pl=3)"]]a swamp near Kisumu[[elif test="is(pl=4)"]]a forest block near Kakamega[[elif test="is(pl=5)"]]a plot of land in Nakuru[[else]]a ranch near Narok[[/if]] is drawn on a grid of \(1\,\text{cm}\) squares. {@nm@} counts \({@F@}\) full squares and \({@P@}\) part squares.</p><p>(a) Estimate the area of the outline in squares.</p><div>[[input:ans1]] squares [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) What real length, in metres, does the side of one square stand for?</p><div>[[input:ans2]] \(\text{m}\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) What real area does one square stand for?</p><div>[[input:ans3]] \(\text{m}^2\) [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Estimate the area of [[if test="is(pl=0)"]]the compound of a school in Machakos[[elif test="is(pl=1)"]]a shamba near Nyeri[[elif test="is(pl=2)"]]a tea farm near Kericho[[elif test="is(pl=3)"]]a swamp near Kisumu[[elif test="is(pl=4)"]]a forest block near Kakamega[[elif test="is(pl=5)"]]a plot of land in Nakuru[[else]]a ranch near Narok[[/if]] in hectares (\(1\) hectare \(= 10\,000\,\text{m}^2\)), correct to 2 decimal places.</p><div>[[input:ans4]] ha [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Each part square counts as half a square: \({@F@} + \tfrac{1}{2} \times {@P@} = {@est@}\) squares.</p><p>(b) \(1\,\text{cm}\) on the map stands for \({@Sd@}\,\text{cm}\) on the ground, which is \({@Sd@} \div 100 = {@side@}\,\text{m}\).</p><p>(c) A square on the map stands for a square on the ground, so square the real length of its side: \({@side@} \times {@side@} = {@sqd@}\,\text{m}^2\).</p><p>(d) Area \(\approx {@est@} \times {@sqd@} = {@hm2d@}\,\text{m}^2\). Divide by \(10\,000\) to change to hectares: about \({@dispdp(float(ha2),2)@}\) ha, correct to 2 decimal places.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
