  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Area Approximations: area of a plot from a map grid</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.2 (a) / Essential 2.1 (a): Estimate an area by counting squares on a map grid, find the real area one square stands for from the scale, and give the area in hectares.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Section A of Chapter 21 (map scale) of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Foundation 2 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2007: the ratio-scale idea combined with counting squares on a map grid; new Kenyan contexts and numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
